==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kai, type μ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Kai μ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kai is a very tough and durable tank unit, especially against Floating enemies. Despite her short range, Kai is extremely useful to stop slow and strong Floating enemies such as the [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird Cat]] for a while and inflict good damage. Her DPS may seem incredible, but due to her short range and long attack animation, she'll often only get a couple hits in before she gets knocked back or defeated. This also undermines the utility of her Survive ability, as unless she is up against an LD enemy with a sizable blindspot like [[Queen B]] or [[Henry]], she cannot make use of it at all. At the very least, though, she has the stats to tank and OHKO a group of [[Brollow]]s.

Kai's usage against non-Floating enemies is limited, as well as many Floating enemies in the game having a non-Floating backliner that punishes the player for using a frontline tank like Kai. Since most Floating enemies have another trait and may inflict status effects (such as [[Maawth]]), they may inflict said debuffs onto her.

Despite being resistant to Floating, it is not recommended to use her against any floating [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] other than [[The Perfect Cyclone]] as her short range and their extreme DPS will simply demolish her in seconds.

Her [[Cat Combo|Combo]], [[Pork on Rice (Combo)|Pork on Rice]], is a good Defence Combo. [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] and Kai both have good uses on certain stages, and it has good synergy with other Combos like [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] or [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart?]].

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Kai μ doubles her health and speed, along with gaining more damage. This makes her especially good against [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemies]], even more so than before. Her newfound knockback immunity now allows her to be a powerful asset in stages such as [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 39|Floor 39]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], where [[Mr. Mole]] would easily knock her back.

Her base stats improve more than significantly, meaning that her previous strengths in her Normal and Evolved forms are exemplified. This True Form is a massive improvement over her previous forms, giving you an even better reason to bring her into battle. Furthermore, her generalist usage is now decent, and along with being able to tank fairly well against non-Floating enemies, makes her damage output worth it for her cost. However, in late [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]] and [[Uncanny Legends]], this means nearly nothing against most peons, as most have enough sheer DPS to end her quickly.

==='''Talents'''===
Presumably due to her already tremendous pool of health, Kai was not given a Defense Buff as a normal Talent. Unfortunately, most of what she got instead isn't too great; Resist Slow and Weaken are about as useful as they always are, and while Resist Wave can make her a decent anti-[[Wave Attack|Wave]] unit, better options for that already exist plentifully. Attack Buff is a little bit better, as her attack power is already quite high, but the NP investment isn't likely to be worth it when [[Catseye]]s are still an option.

While her [[Shield Piercing]] talent may seem great, she has several flaws to make use out of this talent. Her low range combined with her long foreswing means she'll struggle to get hits on even standstill enemies due to peons getting in the way, and with additions like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar]], the talent is rather redundant and only shines the most in [[The Aku Realms]] and in [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|Aku Cyclone's stage]]. If you own better Shield Piercers, this talent can safely be ignored unless you're going for her Ultra Talents. In the case of full investment, Shield Piercing becomes an incredibly useful asset, as with her Ultra Talents she's able to endure Aku attacks long enough to retaliate with her absurdly high damage, enough to wipe the floor with even buffed [[Fallen Bear]]s in a single hit. This, however, does not stop peons from getting in the way of her; be careful to send her out only when appropriate if you want to utilize this talent.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Divine Kai μ's Ultra Talents elevate her role as a frontline tank with critical new utilities. Beyond her core upgrades, she now gains Aku targeting, curse immunity, and a 20% HP boost, refining her niche in high-pressure battles.

The ability to target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]] gives Kai another trait to exploit, excelling against both Floating and Aku threats. This synergy allows her to endure prolonged engagements in Aku-heavy stages like [[Dead Heat Land]] and even [[Heinous Road (Brutal)|Heinous Road]]. While her short range and attack animation still leave her prone to miss to high knockback Aku foes (e.g., [[Aku Doge]], [[Aku Gory]] or any other peons), her survivability ensures she can stall and chip away at sturdy ones, such as [[Le'Behemoth]] or Fallen Bear. Combining Kai with anti-Aku specialists counteracts her limitations, empowering her to withstand mixed assaults from Aku and Floating swarms.

[[Immune to Curse]] solidifies Kai's reliability in chaotic battles. While rare among Aku enemies ([[Malevolent Dark Cat]] being the exception), there are a number of Relic-Floating hybrids for her to tank, such as Golem Sunfish. Furthermore, enemies with [[Curse]] frequently appear in mixed-trait stages featuring Relic foes. For example, in stages like [[Confront the Tyrant]] (Relic + Floating) or [[Queen Mother V]]'s Onslaught, Kai can safely tank curses that would otherwise disable other units. This immunity also future-proofs her against potential curse-heavy Aku variants introduced in updates.

The 20% [[Special Abilities#Stat Enhancements|Defense Buff]] provides a modest increase to her base health, which is particularly valuable for a stat-focused tank unit like Kai, as it allows her to survive longer on the battlefield. However, the steep NP cost to max this talent (10 levels) makes it a luxury upgrade. Prioritize this only after investing in her Aku targeting and Curse Immunity, or if your roster lacks specialized Aku tanks.

===Orb===
An obvious first choice would be a Floating Resistant Up Orb to further augment her abilities, which can be later supplemented by an Aku Resistant Up Orb if her Ultra Talents are factored in.

