==Trivia==
*She first became available alongside [[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Kuu]] and [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Coppermine]] on May 14th, 2014.
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Kai the [[Survive]] ability.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Kai was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Journey to the West (Removed Combo)|Journey to the West]] and [[Curves (Removed Combo)|Curves]].
*The "Uribo" in the Boarborg's Japanese name, Uriborg, is derived from the Japanese word ''uribō'', meaning "young wild boar".
*The μ in her Evolved/True Form's name is the Greek letter "mu".
*Prior to [[Version 14.0 Update|Version 14.0]], Divine Kai μ's description mistakenly referred to the [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait as "Flying".
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], Kai's True Form's name lacked the "μ" part in BCEN.
*Divine Kai μ's Equip and [[Upgrade Menu]] icons both clearly depict her with a wide smile, yet no such expression can be seen in any of her animations.
*She is the first [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] to have two variants: [[Frosty Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Frosty Kai]] and [[Seashore Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Seashore Kai]].
*Due to hopping with Tonton, Kai is one of the only units in her set that doesn't appear to float, the other being [[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa the Lioness]].
*Kai is the name of a female samurai who served under Hojo Ujisayu.
*She is supposed to be modelled after [[wikipedia:Zhu Bajie|Zhu Bajie/Cho Hakkai]] from ''[[wikipedia:Journey to the West|Journey to the West]]'', with Kuu and Coppermine also representing [[wikipedia:Sun Wukong|other]] [[wikipedia:Sha Wujing|characters]]. This is further supported by the fact that Kai, Kuu and Coppermine were once in a combo that went by the same name as the novel. Her portrayal is the least explicit amongst the other [[Cyber Academy Galaxy Gals (Gacha Event)|Galaxy Gals]].
*Kai's oversized hat, predominantly yellow outfit and especially hair style and colour are reminiscent of [[wikia:dragonquest:Alena (Dragon Quest IV)|Alena]] from the ''Dragon Quest'' series. Her being a strong melee unit as well as having an apparent inability to float like the rest of the Galaxy Gals may also reference Alena's combat preference and incapability of using magic.

